1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,960
Sailing Home.
航行回家。

2
00:00:02,960 --> 00:00:35,920
This novel was about an unbelievable but genuine adventure. Its author was a black businessman who was brought up in America. In 1956, he visited Africa, his birthplace.
这部小说讲述了一段难以置信却真实的冒险。作者是一位在美国长大的黑人商人。1956年，他访问了非洲，那是他的出生地。

3
00:00:35,920 --> 00:01:35,313
One day, when he was wandering on the pavement near the bay enjoying the sea scenes, he lost his money and passport that he kept in an envelope. So he went to the embassy to seek help, but the ambassador with rude manners didn’t permit his staff to help though he bowed to him. Staring at his impatient face, he understood that it was the fault of his skin colour that accounted for their rejection.
一天，他在海湾附近的人行道上漫步，欣赏海景，却弄丢了装在信封里的钱和护照。于是他去大使馆寻求帮助，但态度粗鲁的大使不允许工作人员帮助他，尽管他向大使鞠躬恳求。看着大使不耐烦的脸，他明白，对方介意的是他的肤色，这正是他们拒绝帮助的原因。

4
00:01:35,313 --> 00:02:06,140
So he decided to take a chance to sail on a small boat home. He met a large amount of difficulty but was never stopped. On the contrary, difficulty pushed him to go ahead harder.
所以，他决定冒险，乘一条小船航行回家。他遇到了许多困难，但始终没有停下。恰恰相反，困难促使他更加努力地前进。

5
00:02:06,140 --> 00:02:32,800
Three months later, he was spotted by a ship by accident. He was in rags indeed. A maid even screamed when bringing him a steak and pineapple dessert.
三个月后，一艘船偶然发现了他。他的确已是衣衫褴褛。一名女服务员给他送牛排和菠萝甜点时，甚至惊叫起来。

6
00:02:32,800 --> 00:02:58,293
Aboard, he earned his passage by working as a barber and got home finally. As for the name of his novel, he couldn’t think of a better one than the phrase “Go Ahead”.
在船上，他靠做理发师挣得船费，终于回到了家。至于这部小说的名字，他想不出比“勇往直前”更好的名字了。
